)

The split between `mcts.py` and the native core is worth understanding early,
because the two searches serve different masters. The interactive search
optimises *latency*: one position, answer as fast as possible. Self-play
optimises *throughput*: thousands of games at once, and no single game cares how
long it waits. They implement the same algorithm and are tested against each
other, but almost none of the code is shared.

